From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nss-dp: give file-local helpers internal linkage, declare
 syn_ptp_get_tx_hwtstamp_by_id

Linux 6.10 turned on -Wmissing-prototypes and qca-nss-dp builds with
-Werror, so every global definition without a visible prototype fails.
The ipq95xx build only includes the edma_v2 HAL, so the affected files
are the ones below.

Internal linkage (no caller outside the defining file; the edma_v3
ppeds files carry their own static copies of the same names, so there
is no cross-object dependency):

  nss_dp_netstandby.c  3 helpers (nss_dp_get_and_register_cb() is
                       EXPORT_SYMBOL'd, and EXPORT_SYMBOL expands to a
                       non-static declaration, so it keeps external
                       linkage and gets a local prototype instead)
  edma_v2/edma_ppeds.c 13 ppeds ops used only by the local ops table
  hal/gmac_ops/qcom/qcom_if.c  qcom_get_strset_count, qcom_get_strings
                       (referenced only from qcom_nss_gmac_hal_ops)

edma_tx.c calls syn_ptp_get_tx_hwtstamp_by_id(), which is defined in
syn_ptp.c with no header declaration; add it to syn_ptp.h next to the
other exported PTP entry points.  edma_tx.c keeps its local extern,
which is now redundant but harmless.

  qcom_if.c:233/252, nss_dp_netstandby.c:38/64/105/260,
  edma_ppeds.c:852/900/1132/1165/1189/1210/1231/1247/1289/1392/1510/1567/1692,
  syn_ptp.c:2160: error: no previous prototype [-Werror=missing-prototypes]

---
